Hi

Simon Potter and I did some
digging in 'gtable' (to get the new 'ggplot2' plots to export properly
with 'gridSVG') and we found a few things we'd like to comment on ...

- a request:  could 'gtable' please export a gtable_grob() function or
somesuch that creates a gTree from a gtable (most of the current body of
grd.draw.gtable()) ?

- a suggestion:  grid.draw.gtable() currently creates an object with
class of either "gtableParent" or c("gtableParent", "gtableChild").  The
former has just a preDrawDetails() method (to push its 'layoutvp'), but
the latter has a grid.draw() method (to push its 'wrapvp' first), which
is a bit awkward.  If the latter class was instead c("gtableChild",
"gtableParent"), then you could have a
preDrawDetails.gtableParent() method to push the 'layoutvp' and  a
preDrawDetails.gtableChild() method to push the 'wrapvp' then just
NextMethod().  (?)

(first post to a Google Group so apologies for any etiquette breaking)

Paul

