Yes, I agree. I don't like my implementation but this is the easiest way I could find...

> One option might be to enforce a 'vp' of NULL for "gtableChild" objects (via a validDetails() method);

But a child of gtable may be gtable, and vp cannot be NULL in this case.

> alternatively, could you use a grid.draw.gtableParent() method (even though it is not strictly necessary) just to make things a bit more consistent ?

Probably.

Or, can drawGTree have a kind of hook function before calling pushvpgp(x), say, prePushVpgp(x)?

kohske

